    "title": "After the last law",
    "text": "The city did not become fair forever. A later council would make different mistakes. People would again confuse a familiar voice with a reliable answer, or a beautiful promise with a workable plan. What changed was the number of people able to question a record, describe a risk, and insist on a reason. Mira had entered Namar hoping that good work would speak for itself. She left the meeting knowing that good work needs people who can explain it and institutions willing to hear them.\n\nYour vocabulary can grow in the same ordinary way. The next useful step is small: choose a chapter, close the book, and tell its story in your own words. When a word fails to come, look again. When it comes easily, place it in a different situation. Let the city fade if it must. Keep the language you can now use to describe the world outside it.",
